node_modules
# Keep environment variables out of version control.
#
# Ignore every .env variant and re-admit only the example, rather than adding
# suffixes to a list as they turn up. That list was how `.env.bak` slipped
# through: db:set-password writes it before overwriting .env, so it holds the
# *previous* DATABASE_URL, password and all, and nothing was ignoring it.
# Committing a file with a database password in it is how commit decb964
# leaked the last one.
.env*
!.env.example

/generated/prisma
